From c7112a46e2538955e7676aa72137a680594851f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:45:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(wcs): store WCS axis flips; refuse post and generation
 by name

Part 1 of the reversed-axis work. The WCS page gets Flip X, Flip Y and
Flip Z toggles under the turns. Each click is one undoable SetWcsFlip
command. The flags ride the setup's WCS entity (schema::WcsFlip), go to
the project file as an optional "flip" key (PROJECT_VERSION 62), move
with delete/undo and the CreateSetup datum transfer, and show reversed
on the gizmo.

No posted G-code changes. A flipped WCS is refused by name at
collect_job (generation) and in the post verification gate, until the
flip is cleared. The MCP tool set_wcs_flip sets the flags; get_job
shows them under wcs.flip.

Pinned by crates/app/tests/wcs_flip.rs (10 tests) and
egui_app::wcs_flip_tests (3 tests).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Fixes #1720
